<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="94c49e08">The benefits manager has visibility into the portfolio of programs and projects and works closely with the sponsors,
program managers, and project managers throughout the course of the engagement. The benefits manager specializes in
selecting the appropriate benefits management method for a given client context. Using this knowledge and general
facilitation skills, the benefits manager conducts workshops to identify potential benefits and guides the benefits
quantification process. The benefits manager plays a key role in building the business case and the benefits realization
plan as well as in designing the required tracking mechanisms to report progress to the stakeholders. The benefits manager
works to see that the benefits realization plan is executed correctly and that the benefits are reviewed regularly
according to the established review schedule. Finally, the benefits manager works with the program manager during the
program closure phase to verify that proper ownership for any remaining actions, which may be needed so that the
realization of the benefits are transitioned to business as usual (BAU).</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="3c0d13e9"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e3f8267a"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="6eaa0215"></attribute>
<attribute name="skills" nodeId="42a917b">&lt;p&gt;
    A benefits manager needs to have the following knowledge, skills, and abilities:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Expertise in identifying and understanding business drivers, investment objectives, potential benefits,
        organizational changes needed to realize the benefits, and the associated change enablers.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ability to clearly articulate the needs that are associated to the key problem being solved or the initiative being
        taken.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ability to collaborate effectively with the stakeholders through working sessions, workshops, joint application
        design (JAD) sessions and other techniques.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Experience with facilitating all the phases of the benefits management lifecycle with various program
        stakeholders.  Ability to integrate benefits management with other management frameworks such as program
        management, change management, enterprise architecture, etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Knowledge of benefits management best practices, methodologies, and standards and the ability to apply these in the
        appropriate context.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Good communication skills, both verbal and written.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Knowledge of business and technology domains or the ability to quickly understand and synthesize such information.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="assignmentApproaches" nodeId="e07b20aa">This role is at times played by the program manager.</attribute>
